:INFO: Test EVPN Type-2 MAC-only route advertisement and installation using BGP.
:INFO: This testcase is based on Type2-evpn.ut.
:INFO: Only the MAC-only form of EVPN Type-2 is exercised. MAC+IP Type-2 is intentionally not tested.

:PRINT: Topology - cross_link_topology
:PRINT: H1 is attached to PE R0 and H2 is attached to PE R3.
:PRINT: R0 and R3 exchange EVPN routes using iBGP.
:PRINT:
:PRINT: H1 ---- R0 ================= R3 ---- H2
:PRINT:              BGP EVPN
:PRINT:

:CMD: config node R0 interface loopback lo0
:CMD: config node R0 router-id 122.1.1.0
:CMD: config node R0 interface loopback lo0 ip-address 122.1.1.0 32
:CMD: config node R0 protocol isis interface all
:CMD: config node R0 protocol isis source-packet-routing mpls
:CMD: config node R0 protocol isis source-packet-routing mpls node-sid 1000
:CMD: config node R0 protocol isis redistribute connected

:CMD: config node R3 interface loopback lo0
:CMD: config node R3 router-id 122.1.1.3
:CMD: config node R3 interface loopback lo0 ip-address 122.1.1.3 32
:CMD: config node R3 protocol isis interface all
:CMD: config node R3 protocol isis source-packet-routing mpls
:CMD: config node R3 protocol isis source-packet-routing mpls node-sid 1003
:CMD: config node R3 protocol isis redistribute connected

:INFO: Base Config done

:CMD: config node R0 no protocol isis interface eth1
:CMD: config node R0 no interface ethernet eth1 ip-address 192.168.0.2 24
:CMD: config node R0 no interface ethernet eth1 vrf 0
:CMD: config node R0 distributed-anycast-gateway 00:02:00:02:00:02
:CMD: config node R0 bridge-domain 10
:CMD: config node R0 interface ethernet eth1 switchport
:CMD: config node R0 bridge-domain 10 member eth1 encapsulation dot1q 10

:CMD: config node R3 no protocol isis interface eth1
:CMD: config node R3 no interface ethernet eth1 ip-address 192.168.0.2 24
:CMD: config node R3 no interface ethernet eth1 vrf 0
:CMD: config node R3 distributed-anycast-gateway 00:02:00:02:00:02
:CMD: config node R3 bridge-domain 10
:CMD: config node R3 interface ethernet eth1 switchport
:CMD: config node R3 bridge-domain 10 member eth1 encapsulation dot1q 10

:CMD: config node H1 no interface ethernet eth1 ip-address 172.168.0.2 24
:CMD: config node H1 interface ethernet eth1 ip-address 172.168.0.1 24
:CMD: config node H1 rtm-route prefix 0.0.0.0/0 0 0 0 2 0 gateway 172.168.0.254 interface eth1

:CMD: config node H2 rtm-route prefix 0.0.0.0/0 0 0 0 2 0 gateway 172.168.0.254 interface eth1

:CMD: debug node R0 protocol evpn install bridge-domain 10 route ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff mpls-label 144 17003
:CMD: debug node R3 protocol evpn install bridge-domain 10 route ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff mpls-label 144 17000

:INFO: Finally BGP Config

:CMD: config node R0 protocol bgp 65000 neighbor 122.1.1.3 remote-as 65000
:CMD: config node R0 protocol bgp 65000 neighbor 122.1.1.3 address-family l2vpn-evpn
:CMD: config node R0 protocol l2vpn evpn instance 1
:CMD: config node R0 protocol l2vpn evpn instance 1 bridge-domain 10

:CMD: config node R3 protocol bgp 65000 neighbor 122.1.1.0 remote-as 65000
:CMD: config node R3 protocol bgp 65000 neighbor 122.1.1.0 address-family l2vpn-evpn
:CMD: config node R3 protocol l2vpn evpn instance 1
:CMD: config node R3 protocol l2vpn evpn instance 1 bridge-domain 10

:INFO: Test 1 - Generate a MAC-only EVPN Type-2 advertisement from H2.
:INFO: The resulting host MAC must be advertised as a MAC-only Type-2 route; no IP address is expected in the EVPN NLRI.
:CMD: run node H2 resolve-arp 172.168.0.4 source-ip-address 172.168.0.5 src-mac ff:ff:ff:ff:01:05 interface eth1

:INFO: Test 2 - Verify that R0 receives the EVPN Type-2 route through BGP and stores it in the EVPN global RIB.
:INFO: Expected: an EVPN Type-2 MAC-only route for MAC ff:ff:ff:ff:01:05 is present on R0, learned from BGP neighbor 122.1.1.3.
:CMD: show node R0 protocol bgp global-rib l2vpn-evpn

:INFO: Test 3 - Verify that the learned remote MAC is installed in bridge-domain 10 on R0.
:INFO: Expected: MAC ff:ff:ff:ff:01:05 is present as a remote EVPN MAC entry.
:CMD: show node R0 bridge-domain 10

:INFO: Test 4 - Verify end-to-end L2 forwarding after MAC-only Type-2 advertisement.
:INFO: Expected: traffic from H1 to H2 succeeds.
:CMD: run node H1 ping source-address 172.168.0.1 172.168.0.2
